#question(title: [Proving a theorem], centered: true)[
  #slide-block(title: [Theorem])[
    Let $f$ be a function with domain $D$.
    - IF $f$ is increasing on $display(D)$
    - THEN $f$ is one-to-one on $display(D)$
  ]

  #v(1fr)

  + Remind yourself of the precise definition
    of “increasing" and “one-to-one".
  + To prove the theorem, what will you
    assume? what do you want to show?
  + Look at the part you want to show. Based
    on the definition, what is the structure
    of the proof?
  + Complete the proof.
]
